# Generated and transient investigation state.
#
# Two layouts are listed throughout this file. 2.10.0 renamed the workspace's
# directories - sources/ became input/, outputs/ became output/, and runs/,
# snapshots/ and staging/ moved under .ak/ - but this template kept only the older
# names, so every workspace initialized since then ignored none of what it created.
# On a real project that left production .mdb files untracked-but-not-ignored inside
# an application repository. Both layouts stay listed for the same reason the bundle
# readers do: upgrading the kit must not strand a run already in progress.

# 2.10.0 layout
.ak/snapshots/
.ak/staging/
.ak/runs/
output/drafts/
output/render-cache/

# Pre-2.10.0 layout
runs/
outputs/drafts/
outputs/render-cache/

**/__pycache__/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.log
*.laccdb
*.ldb

# Credentials and local connection material
.env
.env.*
*.dsn
secrets/
credentials/

# Raw Access databases can contain production data. Keep them local by default.
# The extensions are spelled in both cases on purpose: this kit's own target
# population ships files named .MDB as often as .mdb, and an ignore rule that only
# matches one case is the kind that looks right and silently is not.
input/access/*.mdb
input/access/*.MDB
input/access/*.accdb
input/access/*.ACCDB
input/access/*.adp
input/access/*.ADP
sources/access/*.mdb
sources/access/*.MDB
sources/access/*.accdb
sources/access/*.ACCDB
sources/access/*.adp
sources/access/*.ADP

# Keep canonical extracted evidence and accepted outputs trackable. The sealed
# bundle under .ak/bundles/ is deliberately absent from every rule above: it is the
# evidence a later phase cites, and it belongs in history.
!extracted/**
!output/*.md
!output/*.html
!output/*.pptx
!output/*.json
!output/*.csv
!outputs/*.md
!outputs/*.html
!outputs/*.pptx
!outputs/*.json
!outputs/*.csv
